formatted_question:
According to the paper "Parameter-Efficient Orthogonal Finetuning via Factorization", in the discussion of orthogonality constraints and counting edges between adjacent levels, for a $d\times d$ orthogonal matrix with $d$ non-zero entries, what can those entries only be?
(A) 0 \text{ or } 1
(B) e^{i\theta}
(C) any non-zero real values
(D) \pm \tfrac{1}{\sqrt{d}}
(E) $\pm 1 $.

