raw_knowledge_statement:
We train a small byte-level auto-regressive language model on the training data for {\textsc BLT} and compute next byte entropies under the LM distribution $p_{e}$ over the byte vocabulary $\mathcal{V}$:

\begin{equation}
H(x_i) = \sum_{v \in \mathcal{V}} p_{e}(x_i=v|\pmb{x}_{<i}) \log p_{e}(x_i=v|\pmb{x}_{<i})
\end{equation}

We train a small byte-level auto-regressive language model on the training data for {\textsc BLT} and compute next byte entropies under the LM distribution $p_{e}$ over the byte vocabulary $\mathcal{V}$:

\begin{equation}
H(x_i) = \sum_{v \in \mathcal{V}} p_{e}(x_i=v|\pmb{x}_{<i}) \log p_{e}(x_i=v|\pmb{x}_{<i})
\end{equation}

For each step $i$, we first construct byte-grams

\begin{align}
    g_{i,n}=\{b_{i-n + 1},\ldots, b_i\}
\end{align}

for each byte position $i$ and $n$ from three to eight.

For each step $i$, we first construct byte-grams

\begin{align}
    g_{i,n}=\{b_{i-n + 1},\ldots, b_i\}
\end{align}

for each byte position $i$ and $n$ from three to eight.

We calculate the augmented embedding

\begin{align}
e_i &= x_i + \sum_{n = 3,...,8}E_{n}^{hash}(\text{Hash}(g_{i,n})) \\
\text{where, Hash}(g_{i,n}) &= \text{RollPolyHash}(g_{i,n}) \% |E_{n}^{hash}|
\end{align}

formatted_question:
In the paper "Byte Latent Transformer: Patches Scale Better Than Tokens", when the authors define Bits-Per-Byte (BPB) as the tokenizer-independent version of perplexity for comparing byte and token-level models, what quantity appears in the numerator of the BPB fraction?
(A) \mathrm{PPL}(\pmb{x})
(B) \mathcal{H}(\pmb{x})
(C) \mathcal{L}_{CE}(\pmb{x})
(D) \ln(2)\cdot n_{\text{bytes}}
(E) \text{FL}_{\text{{\textsc BLT}}}

raw_knowledge_statement:
Specifically:

\begin{align}
    \text{BPB}(x)&= \frac{\mathcal{L}_{CE}(\pmb{x})}{\ln(2)\cdot n_{\text{bytes}}}
\end{align}

where the uncertainty over the data $\pmb{x}$ as measured by the sum of the cross-entropy loss is normalized by the total number of bytes in $\pmb{x}$ and a constant.

